===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres_ptc_qual=US|pres_ptc2=basinning|past_qual=US|past2=basinned}}

# To create a concavity or depression in.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1925|month=June|work=Proceedings of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences|title=The Geology of Ascension Island |author=Reginald A. Daly|volume=60|number=1|passage=Then axial subsidence '''basined''' the surface of the dome.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=The Numismatist - Volume 116, Issues 7-12 |author=|page=21 |ISBN=|passage='''Basining''' is the process that gives the faces of the dies their radius, or concavity. Depending on the production method, the planchet metal flows either toward or away from the center of the dies. The minting facilities "'''basined'''" the dies after they  were delivered from the Philadelphia Mint's Engraving Department. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|title=The Complete Guide to Lincoln Cents |author=David W. Lange |page=8 |ISBN=|passage=Of course, this is exactly what did happen—the antiquated practice of '''basining''' the dies was cast aside for the Lincoln Cent.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=Symphony of the Earth |author=Johannes Herman Frederik Umbgrove |page=47 |ISBN=|passage=Scandinavia was '''basined''' under the load of the last or so-called Würm ice-cap.}}
# To serve as or become a basin.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976 |title=Monographiae Biologicae - Volume 30 |author=Günther Kunkel |page= 77|ISBN=|passage=To what degree this stress field formed in response to eastward movement of the African plate, to northward movement of the African plate relative to Europe, to '''basinning''' of the shelf between the eastern Canaries and Africa, or to other causes is as yet unknown.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992 |title=Geologic field guide to the Columbia River |author=John H. Bush; W. Patrick Seward|page=9 |ISBN=|passage=The eastward pinching and thinning were caused by the rapid '''basining''' of the plateau over the Pasco-Richland area in south-central Washington.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009 |title=Shifting Sands: The Archaeology of Sand Hollow |author=Richard K. Talbot; Lane D. Richens |page=90 |ISBN=|passage=Walls '''basined''' at a ca. 45° angle on the southwest side, but on the west and north there was little '''basining''', with the floor sloping gently up to the original ground surface. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Strain Facies |author=E. Hansen |page=133 |ISBN=|passage=Deformation of the rocks involved in anticline formation increased as deformation of the rocks involved in '''basining''' decreased, and the less intense structures of the norfold facies developed in both regions.}}
# To shelter or enclose in a basin.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888 |title=The Genesis of Queensland|author=Henry Stuart Russell |page= |ISBN=|passage=A moan as of distant wind or thunder portended something at hand, the approach of which, '''basinned''' as we were among high broken ridges, patchy-scrubbed heights, and penned in by a maze of steep-sided gullies or gorges — we had no chance of observing, until it cam down in hurricane strength.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1920|title=Bulletin of the U.S. Department of Agriculture |author=|page= 16|ISBN=|passage=A row of trees was '''basined''' in the latter part of April, and by the latter part of July, a little over three months, there was a remarkable improvement in the appearance of the basined row compared with the check trees.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|title=Quest - Volumes 13-19 |author=|page=28 |ISBN=|passage= Caesar's subjects bathed in Caesar's blood '''basinned''' in the purple pool of Calpurnia's dream; my sister slept in an ogre's thought and woke up on the hook of a cannibal finger. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=The Legal Studies Forum - Volume 31 |author=|page=1103 |ISBN=|passage=They took a narrow path through the snow, up the hill which '''basined''' the village, and on to a plateau, a stretch of sparsely treed land.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=An Apache Princess: A Tale of the Indian Frontier |author=Charles King |page=173 |ISBN=|passage=Well back under this natural shelter, '''basined''' in the hollowed rock, a blessed pool of fair water lay unwrinkled by even a flutter of breeze.}}

